# Words Folders says when it runs without the other parts of Trindle it sometimes needs.

## Missing parts (src/files/alone.rs)

# Red note when a folder is shared and Trindle's own helper is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-share = Sharing a folder needs a Trindle helper program that isn't installed.
# Note when a Windows share is opened and Trindle's own helper is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-mount = Opening a Windows share needs a Trindle helper program that isn't installed.
# Note when an NFS export is opened and Trindle's own helper is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-nfs = Opening an NFS share needs a Trindle helper program that isn't installed.
# Red note when the wallpaper is set from Folders and Trindle's wallpaper program is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-wallpaper = Setting the wallpaper needs Trindle's wallpaper program, which isn't installed.
# Red note when a folder is opened as administrator and the program that asks for the administrator password is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-root = Opening a folder as administrator needs pkexec, which isn't installed.
# Red note when a folder is shared with AI programs and Trindle's program for that is not on this computer.
folders-alone-no-ai = Sharing with AI programs needs a Trindle program that isn't installed.
# Red note when a folder is opened in a terminal and none is installed.
folders-alone-no-terminal = There's no terminal installed to open this folder in.
